---
description: Minimal diffs, local style, no drive-by fixes
alwaysApply: true
---

- Writing: use hyphen (-); never em dash (—).
- Change only what the task needs. No drive-by cleanup, renames, or refactors.
- Out of scope: tell the user; do not fix unless asked.
- Match local style in the area you edit; do not import foreign patterns.
- In touched code only, remove orphans/duplicates left by your change.
- Prefer simple, performant code; avoid needless complexity.
